  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><blockquote><p><img src=\"assets\\st0209_55562221e8e9.png\" style=\"width: 390px; height: 157px;\" /></p><p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the refractive indices of the air and optical fibre respectively.&nbsp;Applying Snell&#39;s law at Q, we get:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><msup><mn>40</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4885</mn><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></math></p><p>The distance covered along the length of the optical fibre after one&nbsp;reflection:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>QN</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>RN</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>cot&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>cot</mi><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>The reflections&nbsp;take place throughout&nbsp;the length of the optical fibre.</p><p>Length of the wire<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Total number of reflections along its length<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Length</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>the</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>wire</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>distance</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>covered</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>one</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>reflection</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>along</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>the</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>length</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100000</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>57735</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>57000</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>"
  }
